1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
From the email to the booking. Two tools, two jobs.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Part one. What Deckhand does. It takes the identifiers out of the email. Nothing else.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:32,000
This is the job. Two container numbers, two seal numbers, and they have to reach INTTRA without a typo.

4
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Deckhand is in the sidebar, under Invoices. Nothing is saved here: it reads the document and forgets it.

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Select the whole email and paste it. Headers, signature, all of it. Then press Extract.

6
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Four cards come back. The paste-ready block is the one you copy from.

7
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Read the block against the email before it goes anywhere. That check is the point, not a formality.

8
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Paired only where the document showed them together. The note in brackets tells you what the evidence was.

9
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Two lists side by side is not evidence. Deckhand will not guess which seal belongs to which container, and neither should you.

10
00:01:47,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Container numbers carry a check digit. A failure is flagged in red, never corrected quietly. Retype it from the source.

11
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Copy all, then paste into INTTRA. In your own browser, in the session you already opened. Deckhand never logs in for you and never sees your password.

12
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Part two. What Tidelane does. It keeps the record. It does not read your email.

13
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Step one, route. Where the cargo is going, and on what terms.

14
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Step two, cargo. Container types and counts.

15
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Step three, sailing. These come from the INTTRA connector, running in mock mode.

16
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Step four, review. Read the small print before you confirm.

17
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Booking confirmed. This writes to Tidelane only. No booking is sent to a carrier.

18
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:06,000
These are Tidelane's own container and seal numbers, not the ones from the email.

19
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Two separate jobs. Deckhand's output goes to INTTRA. Tidelane keeps its own record. When Deckhand gets something wrong: trust the email, not the block.
